              <td style="padding:12px;border:1px solid #5a76a3;">Both people agree on a comfortable and safe plan</td>
              <td style="padding:12px;border:1px solid #5a76a3;">Meeting secretly or in an isolated location</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Red Flags and Scams to Watch For</h2>

      <p>
        Anyone actively looking for a relationship online is also, unfortunately, a target for a
        fairly well-documented set of manipulation tactics. Knowing the common patterns makes them
        much easier to spot.
      </p>

      <h3>Refusal to Video Call or Meet, Ever</h3>

      <p>
        Someone who consistently avoids video calls, always has an excuse, or insists on staying
        in text-only contact for weeks or months is a common pattern in romance-scam behavior.
        A real person interested in a relationship generally has no strong reason to avoid ever
        being seen or heard.
      </p>

      <h3>Fast, Intense Declarations of Feeling</h3>

      <p>
        Expressions of deep love or commitment within days, before any real getting-to-know-you
        period, are a well-documented manipulation tactic designed to build emotional dependency
        quickly. Genuine connection almost always develops more gradually than this.
      </p>

      <h3>Any Request for Money, Gift Cards, or Financial Information</h3>

      <p>
        This is the clearest and most consistent red flag across romance-scam reporting from
        consumer protection agencies. A stranger you've only spoken to online — regardless of how
        long or how convincing the conversation has been — should never be sent money, gift cards,
        cryptocurrency, or financial account details, no matter what story accompanies the request.
      </p>

      <h3>Inconsistent Personal Details</h3>

      <p>
        Stories that shift over time — a changing job, a changing location, explanations that
        don't quite add up when you ask a simple follow-up question — are worth taking seriously
        rather than explaining away.
      </p>

